==Swedish==

===Pronunciation===
['blàt:ɛ]

===Etymology===
The word probably originated from the latin languages meaning “cockroach”. The term “blatte” has taken on pejorative qualities as it implies not only darkness of skin, but a general lack of intelligence and sophistication. The word is used  as a condescending term for people living in an Northern European country that are not of (Northern/Central) European descent.

===Noun===
{{sv-noun|g=c}}

# an often derogatory term for a person living in a Northern European country who is not of European descent.

====Declension====
{{sv-noun-reg-ar|2=blatt}}

